po"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10194876</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-1115888-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>1115888</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1114807A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ABE YUGAKU</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUI AKIRA</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMITAKE KAZUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ABE, YUGAKU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMITAKE, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ABE YUGAKU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUI AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAMITAKE KAZUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ABE, YUGAKU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMITAKE, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A composite material which comprises a three-dimensional ceramic network structure and, placed into crevices of the structure, a component containing a semi-metal which has been molten and then precipitated and has a thermal expansion coefficient of 6 ppm/ DEG C or less and a thermal conductivity of 150 W/m.K or more; and a semiconductor device using the same. The composite material is produced by impregnating a porous material having ceramics as a main constituent with the melt of a component containing a semi-metal, to thereby fill the pore of the porous material with the component. The material can be used for manufacturing a member of a semiconductor device which is light and has a high thermal conductivity, and in particular, has a thermal expansion coefficient similar to those of semiconductor elements and other members arranged adjacent thereto.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce matériau composite comprend une structure de réseau céramique tridimensionnelle, dans les pores de laquelle on a placé un composant contenant un semi-métal que l'on a mis à l'état de fusion puis précipité, ce semi-métal possédant un coefficient d'expansion thermique de l'ordre de 6 ppm/ DEG C ou moins et une conductivité thermique de l'ordre de 150 W/m.K ou davantage. L'invention concerne également un dispositif à semi-conducteur comprenant ce matériau. On produit ce matériau composite en imprégnant un matériau poreux constitué principalement de matières céramiques, avec un composant en fusion contenant un semi-métal, pour remplir les pores du matériau poreux à l'aide de ce composant. On peut utiliser ce matériau pour fabriquer un élément d'un dispositif à semi-conducteur, ce matériau étant léger et possédant une forte conductivité thermique, et notamment un coefficient d'expansion thermique semblable à celui des éléments à semi-conducteur et autres éléments agencés dans son voisinage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>